{
  "id": "L6-F2",
  "severity": "high",
  "problem": "The mpd_ultrawork tool's declared output schema is `planFile: { type: \"string\" }` while the engine returns `planFile: string | null` (null whenever plan=false). The harness's output validator therefore rejects EVERY plan=false result: `Error: tool \"mpd_ultrawork\" returned invalid output: \"value.planFile\" must be a string` — measured live, reproducibly, on both calls of ultrawork-smoke (the model had to read `.mpd/ulw/<id>/state.json` from disk instead of consuming the tool result). plan=false is the DEFAULT for the /ulw command path, so the user-invocable surface this wave ships hands its caller an invalid result. The defect is PRE-EXISTING: `git show HEAD:packages/mpd-ulw-plugin/src/index.ts` carries the identical `schema:` line with `planFile: { type: \"string\" }` and the wave's diff does not touch it; no test covers it (engine.test.ts only asserts planFile truthy on the plan=true path), and ultrawork-smoke greens because it asserts on-disk state, not the tool result.",
  "evidence": null,
  "requiredFix": "Declare the field nullable (e.g. `planFile: { type: [\"string\", \"null\"] }`) or omit it when null, in packages/mpd-ulw-plugin/src/index.ts; add a unit test that validates a plan=false result object against the tool's own declared schema. Note the fix belongs to src (t8 rebuilds dist) and must not be applied by this verification lane."
}

